-- Issue 133: a component whose type is an OCTET STRING (CONTAINING X) type assignment is decoded by a call of that type
-- assignment's decoder, which fails when the contents do not fit the region (uPER: a length of 0 octets; ACN: 2 octets for
-- contents of 18 bits). The Ada
-- decoders of PDU (uPER and ACN, legacy and --acn-v2) classified that call by X, which cannot fail, asserted success
-- and decoded on: the next component overwrote the result and a stream the C decoders reject was accepted.
UPER-WIRE-CONTAINING DEFINITIONS AUTOMATIC TAGS ::= BEGIN
    T   ::= SEQUENCE { a INTEGER (0..255), b BOOLEAN OPTIONAL, c INTEGER (0..255) OPTIONAL }
    Box ::= OCTET STRING (CONTAINING T)
    PDU ::= SEQUENCE { f Box, z BOOLEAN }
END
